  "description": "Installation of a single-storey rear pergola attached to the existing rear elevation. The proposed structure features solid aluminium framing and posts, with a retractable textile roof surface. The pergola will measure 10.8m in width and 4.1m in depth, with a maximum overall height of 2.2m.\n\nThe proposed rear pergola has been carefully designed to ensure it has zero adverse impact on the residential amenity of neighbouring properties. Unlike a solid brick extension, the pergola is an inherently lightweight, open, and permeable structure.\n\nComprising slim, solid aluminium posts and a retractable textile roof surface, the structure allows for maximum light penetration and does not cause any issues regarding overshadowing or loss of daylight to adjacent gardens. Furthermore, as an open-sided structure with a maximum depth of 4.1m, it introduces no solid massing, visual intrusion, or loss of privacy for occupiers of neighbouring plots. The pergola connects seamlessly to the existing rear elevation and maintains a harmonious relationship with both the host dwelling and the private rear garden space.",
